Changes made for round 4 PCB design: 

Changed MOSFET from SSM3K339R,LF to BSS806NH6327XTSA1 for lower on resistance ~250 mohm to ~50 mohm
Changed MOSFET footprint to accomodate for part change and for ease of soldering (SOT23-F to SOT23-3)
Changed JST connector from XH (2.54mm spacing) to PH (2.0 mm spacing) to match solenoids, XH was the wrong connector. 
Removed Zener diodes from motor/solenoid drivers, as testing showed no benefits. 
Changed order of servo connection to match servo pins 
Added bulk capacitance to motor power line
Changed IO from single button to multiple button using a resistor ladder and an ADC pin, added pins to allow for off-PCB buttons
Added series termination resistors to SPI signal lines to increase signal integrity

Schematic and layout shown in figures 7 and 8, respecively. 
